meta {
  name: Device API
  seq: 3
}

docs {
  # Device-facing API

  The endpoints the on-device **orchestrator** calls, nested under
  `{{baseUrl}}/device/…` (plus the unprotected `POST /register`). Included
  for reference and manual testing — during a demo these are exercised by
  the edge devices themselves.

  All `/device/*` routes require a **device JWT**: a token containing
  `"role": "device"` signed with the device's TPM-backed signing key
  (registered during `POST /register`). A user JWT is rejected here, and a
  device JWT is rejected on the user routes — set `{{deviceJwt}}` in the
  environment if you have one.

  Poll loop of the orchestrator: `PUT /ping` → `GET /os` (switch + reboot
  if it differs from the booted image) → `GET /apps` (reconcile
  containers) → `PUT /os`, `PUT /apps` (report actual state) →
  `POST /logs` (ship journal + container logs).
}
